# The behavioural harness's edge.
#
# Two names share one site on purpose. `localhost` is how the test runner reaches
# the proxy from the host (published as 8443), and the second is the public name
# the stack is pretending to have. Both go through the same reverse_proxy, so the
# app's view of the request is a real one rather than a header a test set by hand.
#
# `tls internal` is Caddy's own CA: real TLS termination, with a certificate the
# test client is told to trust rather than one a browser would accept.
https://localhost, https://api.marketcore.test {
	tls internal

	# Caddy rewrites X-Forwarded-For and X-Forwarded-Proto on the way through and
	# leaves the client's Host alone. That is what gives the API something to
	# observe, and what the forwarded-header assertions read back.
	reverse_proxy api:3001
}
